notes={
326097:('parked_source_body_gap','Conjecture 4.8: reduced associated-graded local ring for GL_p x GL_q orbit closures. Source patch equations are themselves conjecturally radical in general (4.4); checking them without that semantic bridge cannot certify every orbit closure.','No new patch-ideal search implemented. Source reports p+q<=7, which is inherited evidence only. Need exact Groebner/radical certificates and patch-to-local-ring bridge; finite polynomial search coverage incomplete.'),
326377:('parked_hard_global_minima','Conjecture 12, not Conjecture 8: gem-complexity =5+2c for p>=3. Source Propositions 10,11 distinguish known classes and conditional bounds.','No new triangulation/crystallization enumeration. Global minimality of both invariants cannot be read from a single triangulation; source catalogue through complexity 5 is not a new search. Finite search coverage incomplete.'),
327574:('parked_sustained_exact_search','Conjecture 4.1 extends Theorem 1.2: short pure-diagram tails for L and (L,x) have identical degree sequences and rational coefficients.','Exhaustive 4,139 ideals through terminal degree7; additional incomplete degree11 sweep 213,155. No counterexample. Residual short-tail invariant for exceptional x(x,y,z^t)+J family remains unproved. See DEEP-ROUTES.md.'),
327993:('parked_algorithmic_scope','Source asks for orientation-reversing self-homeomorphism algorithm for closed orientable irreducible 3-manifolds; hyperbolic case is already handled via outer automorphisms and H3.','No new algorithm. Need oriented JSJ/Seifert/Haken compatibility and termination proof. Small-manifold samples cannot establish or refute existence of a uniform algorithm. Later homeomorphism-algorithm literature not cleared.'),
328316:('parked_analytic_gap','Conjecture 3.7: equality in (3.2), Remark3.3, under Lemma3.2(c). The missing step is nonvanishing of the second asymptotic coefficient of an end of a holomorphic curve.','Not a finite braid enumeration: admissibility includes existence of the holomorphic end. Arbitrary formal braids are not source counterexamples. No full curve analytic construction or proof.'),
328509:('parked_lifting_gap','Source Section9: local G extensions over algebraically closed k of characteristic p, cyclic Sylow, KGB obstruction vanishing implies mixed-characteristic lift. KGB compares genera of all quotient covers.','Finite group tables alone do not decide the existence of a lift of a given formal-power-series action. No ramified-extension enumeration; no sufficiency proof. Cyclic/Oort and small dihedral known cases would be routine specialisations.'),
328683:('excluded_known_followup_lead','Recovered Theorem6.1: cactus-group monodromy agrees with crystal commutor, not merely existence of a cyclic vector. Source conjectures arbitrary semisimple Lie algebra. Halacheva-Kamnitzer-Rybnikov-Weekes arXiv:1708.05105 Theorem1.4 states the arbitrary-g agreement.','Theorem1.4, operadic-covering explanation and later proof framework inspected; full proof chain not reverified. arXiv:1608.04625 cyclicity theorem alone is a distinct claim and was not used as a substitute. No new result claimed; no finite representation sweep after finding direct prior art.'),
329002:('parked_number_field_gap','Source cyclotomic Z5 layers B_5,n class number1 for all positive n. This is exact class number, not only absence of 5-primary torsion.','No new class-group calculation; PARI/gp and Sage absent. Source heuristic probabilities do not prove any additional layer. Need a uniform all-prime class-group argument. Finite computable search coverage incomplete.'),
329103:('parked_infinite_quotient_gap','Source higher-order torsion conjecture: for each knot there is a torsion-free elementary amenable quotient with torsion degree 2g-1.','Searching only abelian/derived-length-bounded quotients cannot refute the existential quantifier over all TFEA groups. No new knot census computation. Need a finite obstruction theorem or a full construction of detecting quotients.'),
330110:('excluded_unfixed_source_semantics','Source Collatz-based number system uses d_i and principal/fundamental sets; MathDB does not give a formal representation relation.','No credit for a paraphrase/domain correction. No source-faithful finite predicate was fixed, and no finite sweep is claimed. Quantified derivability and the complete d_i definition must be specified before meaningful search.'),
330534:('parked_iwasawa_gap','Source Greenberg conjecture is finiteness of X+ in its cyclotomic setup; X- pseudocyclicity is stated as an implication/context, not the defining conjecture.','Finite class groups at finitely many levels do not imply finite inverse-limit module. No new field computations or all-level proof. Need uniform control, not an endpoint example.'),
330606:('parked_sustained_exact_search','Survey Conjecture6 points to Braun-Solus arXiv:1408.4713 and r-stable second-hypersimplex unimodality. Fixed cyclic r-stability and excluded empty/lower-dimensional endpoint misuse.','All 16 full-dimensional pairs n3..9,r1..floor((n-1)/2), exact lattice enumeration t0..n-1; unimodal. Remaining global coefficient injection/real-rootedness mechanism absent. See DEEP-ROUTES.md.'),
330976:('parked_categorical_gap','Source Conjecture8.16 concerns chi_m in equation8.21 for the Heisenberg category built from the stipulated Frobenius superalgebra B. B=F is already proved (Remark8.17).','No finite-dimensional matrix search asserted: diagrammatic source and target are generally infinite-dimensional; a truncation requires a proven faithful bound. Need diagram basis/injectivity and arbitrary-m proof; later categorification basis literature not cleared.'),
331362:('excluded_known_exact_theorem','Tao arXiv:1509.05363 Theorem1.1 proves the exact real/complex Hilbert-space discrepancy assertion. The source 1509.03421 predates that resolution.','Read vector-valued Theorem1.1, equivalent stochastic formulation1.8/1.9 and Fourier reduction explanation. This is exact published prior art, not a deduction from only the scalar theorem. No new finite sequence search needed after direct prior resolution.'),
331657:('parked_abundance_scale','Source compact connected Kahler X: all positive pluricanonical sections vanish iff uniruled. The only-if direction is easy; the converse is presented as an abundance consequence.','No finite instance search can decide rational-curve coverage of arbitrary compact Kahler manifolds. No proof of the hard converse; dimension-zero or non-Kahler loopholes excluded.'),
331705:('candidate_full_lean_root_review_required','Source Conjecture4.7 directly refuted in the Euclidean plane C: G=C\\[1,infinity), center0,r7/4,y4+i,z2+i/2. All topology, full boundary supremum bounds, midpoint and infinity-zero bridge proved.','Full ordinary proof CASSINIAN-ORDINARY-PROOF.md; literal Lean SourceClaim/source_refutation; fresh extraction/rebuild, leanchecker and all-local-declaration audit. Journal source403 remains material review limit; no novelty acceptance. Finite rational search is diagnostic only.'),
332276:('parked_asymptotic_discrepancy','Source higher-order weighted discrepancy is a uniform asymptotic lower bound with positive constant depending on r,d; it contains the classical star-discrepancy difficulty.','No fixed m point-set or choice of a small constant refutes the existence of C(r,d). Need an asymptotic family defeating every positive constant, or the full lower-bound proof. No grid optimisation is represented as an exhaustive conjecture search.'),
332527:('excluded_known_source_theorem_and_metadata_error','Source S(G)=sum_(H<=G) phi(H), phi(H)=number of elements of order exp(H), NOT sum of orders of elements. Correct Conjecture6 is exactly Corollary1.2 of arXiv:1704.03083; proof body read.','26 explicit cyclic/product/dihedral nilpotent groups, all subgroups enumerated, all source inequalities/equality characterizations hold. No claim of all groups up to a size. Literal MathDB error is not counted as a refutation.'),
332535:('parked_continuous_covering_gap','Source cylindrical-covering conjecture for ellipsoids in E^d, 2<k<d. Need normalized k-codimensional cross-sectional volumes in arbitrary cylinder covers, not just balls/axis-aligned cylinders.','No exhaustive search over continuum cylinders claimed. Finite cylinder families need exact cover certificates of the entire body. Slicing/Fubini handles established cases, not an immediate arbitrary-k extension.'),
333757:('excluded_known_exact_followup','Golan-Polak arXiv:2210.03564 Theorem2 and Corollary3 explicitly prove every finite-index subgroup of F is 2-generated, resolving source Conjecture12.6.','Read the stated lifting of an abelianization pair, finite-index normal-subgroup consequence and direct identification of Conjecture12.6. Infinite group generators, not finite group tables; no new result or finite quotient surrogate claimed.')}
for key,v in x.items():
 i=int(key);outcome,scope,attempt=notes[i];v.update(outcome=outcome,source_scope=scope,mathematical_attempts_and_search_coverage=attempt,review_depth='literal_statement_and_targeted_primary_body_read; specific followup depth in notes; not a complete literature audit',history_check='history-matches.txt contains assignment bookkeeping and numeric false positives; no earlier substantive exact-ID review found in the scoped prose/results scan',credit=0,accepted=False,remaining='root independent source fidelity, novelty/significance and acceptance review' if i==331705 else 'No full new exact Lean endpoint; do not count',receipts=[f'sources/{v["source_url"].rsplit("/",1)[-1]}.html.receipt.json'],formal_endpoint='Cassinian331705.source_refutation' if i==331705 else None)
